nodecode-netmind is a rewrite of NetMind-AI's NetMind-AI/netmind-hermes-provider:
https://github.com/NetMind-AI/netmind-hermes-provider
commit 00ab432e251fc04b983382a7b339f54d96e4b29d
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 NetMind AI (LICENSE)

The plugin was one ProviderProfile for Hermes' own provider registry: an
OpenAI-compatible base, a key variable, a roster in fallback_models, an
output cap per model in OUTPUT_LIMITS and a capability per model in
model_capabilities. All of that data was rewritten as a Nodecode provider
cell: one catalog row under the provider id netmind, the chat lane's package
and the section's base, the key read from NETMIND_API_KEY, and the same 31
models with the window, the answer cap, vision, reasoning and tool calls the
plugin declares. A `/netmind` command was added to print the roster, since a
provider cell's roster is otherwise only visible in the model picker. What was
left out is Hermes-side, not data: the profile's alias netmind-ai, its
default_aux_model, and its supports_health_check and supports_model_listing
flags have no counterpart here - Nodecode names a lane through the catalog
row, and a key is saved with /connect and checked by the core's own listing
call. The plugin's Python tests were not carried over; the cell's own tests
stand where they did.
